{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Observations.centered_hecke_variance_positive","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Observations.centered_hecke_variance_positive","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.old_term1_pos_fails_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.old_term1_pos_fails_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/centered_hecke_variance_positive.lean#L138-L149","doc":"**The old convention-C decomposition is not available under D.**\nThe discarded hypothesis `0 < (q - q⁻¹) * z` forces `1 < q`: it is false at\n`q = 1`, where the variance nevertheless attains its minimum `3/4 > 0`.\n\nThis is the concrete witness that the previous encoding's domain was strictly\nsmaller than the `.md`'s. Stated over `ℚ` so it is a closed arithmetic fact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.centeredVariance_eq_three_quarters_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.centeredVariance_eq_three_quarters_iff","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/centered_hecke_variance_positive.lean#L113-L136","doc":"**The minimum is attained exactly at `q = 1`.** For `q ≠ 0`,\n`Var(σᵢ) = 3/4 ↔ q² = 1`.\n\nOver `ℝ` with `q > 0` this is `q = 1` and only there — the `.md`'s claim, which\nthe previous encoding could not state because its `term1_pos` axiom fails\nprecisely at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.three_quarters_le_centeredVariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.three_quarters_le_centeredVariance","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/centered_hecke_variance_positive.lean#L106-L111","doc":"**Lower bound.** `3/4 ≤ Var(σᵢ)` for every `q ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.centeredVariance_sub_three_quarters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.centeredVariance_sub_three_quarters","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/centered_hecke_variance_positive.lean#L98-L104","doc":"**Exact gap to the minimum.** `Var(σᵢ) - 3/4 = (q² - 1)²/(4(q² + 1)²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.centeredVariance_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.centeredVariance_pos","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/centered_hecke_variance_positive.lean#L87-L96","doc":"**Positivity, unconditional.** For every `q ≠ 0`, `0 < Var(σᵢ)`.\n\nNo regime hypothesis is needed: under convention D the closed form is a ratio of\nmanifestly positive polynomials. In particular positivity holds at `q = 1` and\nfor all `q < 1`, both of which the previous class-axiomatised encoding excluded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.centeredVariance_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.centeredVariance_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/centered_hecke_variance_positive.lean#L71-L85","doc":"**Closed form.** `Var(σᵢ) = (q⁴ + q² + 1)/(q² + 1)²`.\n\nThis is the identity the block's `.md` states under convention D.\n\nNo `q ≠ 0` hypothesis is needed. The block reads `q > 0` throughout and `q⁻¹`\nis only meaningful there, but Mathlib's `0⁻¹ = 0` makes both sides equal `1` at\n`q = 0` as well, so the identity is unconditional as stated in Lean. The\nhypothesis was carried in a first draft and removed once the linter showed it\nunused — recorded here so a reader does not re-add it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.sq_add_one_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.sq_add_one_pos","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/centered_hecke_variance_positive.lean#L67-L69","doc":"`q² + 1` is strictly positive in any strict ordered field, so it is a\nlegitimate denominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.centeredVariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.centeredVariance","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/centered_hecke_variance_positive.lean#L62-L65","doc":"The centred Hecke generator is `σ̃ᵢ := σᵢ - z · 1`; its variance under the\nMarkov trace is `Var(σᵢ) = tr_M(σ̃ᵢ²) = (q - q⁻¹) z + 1 - z²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.markovZD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.markovZD","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/centered_hecke_variance_positive.lean#L58-L60","doc":"Markov parameter in **convention D**: `z = q³/(q² + 1)`\n(owner ruling 2026-08-09; convention C `z = 1/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})` excised). ","signatureChunk":0}]}